+## Summary of the fix
+
+The root cause is in `src/_pytest/skipping.py`. `pytest_runtest_makereport` only *read* the cached `xfailed_key` value that had been computed during `pytest_runtest_setup` / `pytest_runtest_call`. When a test adds an `xfail` marker dynamically (via `request.node.add_marker`), that happens *after* those hooks have cached "no xfail", so the dynamically added marker was ignored.
+
+The fix re-evaluates the `xfail` markers in `pytest_runtest_makereport` whenever the cached value is `None`, so dynamically added markers are honored, while preserving the existing caching for statically marked tests.
